# ==============================================================================
# Database: DHCP Option 60 (Vendor Class Identifier - VCI)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Field Schema:
#   Regex Pattern | OS Name | Confidence Score (1-99) | Device Type | Vendor
#
# Rules for Adding Entries:
#   1. Case-insensitive regex is matched against the raw DHCP packet buffer.
#   2. Specific versions/sub-models MUST be placed ABOVE broad vendor matches:
#      (e.g., 'vendor-class.*msft 5\.0 xbox' BEFORE 'vendor-class.*msft').
#   3. Scores are typically high (94-98) due to hardcoded firmware strings.
#
# Example:
#   vendor-class.*steam-?deck|Steam Deck (SteamOS)|98|console|Valve
#   vendor-class.*android-dhcp-1[3-6]|Android|97|smartphone|Android
# ==============================================================================

# ==============================================================================
# Gaming Handhelds & Consoles
# ==============================================================================
vendor-class.*msft 5\.0 xbox|Xbox Gaming Console|98|console|Microsoft
vendor-class.*xbox|Xbox Gaming Console|98|console|1,3,6,15,26
vendor-class.*playstation 5|Sony PlayStation 5|98|console|Sony
vendor-class.*playstation 4|Sony PlayStation 4|98|console|Sony
vendor-class.*playstation|Sony PlayStation Console|98|console|Sony
vendor-class.*ps[45]|Sony PlayStation Console|98|console|Sony
vendor-class.*nintendo switch|Nintendo Switch Console|98|console|Nintendo
vendor-class.*nintendo|Nintendo Switch Console|98|console|Nintendo
vendor-class.*steam-?deck|Steam Deck (SteamOS)|98|console|Valve
vendor-class.*steam|Steam Hardware / Client|92|console|Valve
